{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The third time</b><br>\"My vineyard, which is mine.\" ([She will say: Knesset Yisrael,] \"My vineyard is mine.\") The matter is that all the tribes will return to be together." "\"The thousand, O Solomon, are yours.\" The matter of \"Solomon\" is King Messiah, and he is called so because he is of his family, like \"and David my servant shall be their prince forever\" [Ezekiel 37:25]. And the matter is: then the tribes will return to you, O Solomon, for you are King Messiah, and also the two hundred that belonged to the keepers of its fruit, which Solomon left to his sons, will return."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The parenthetical introduces כנס׳ ישר׳ as an apparent speaker gloss; abbreviations resolved as כנסת ישראל.", 1 "Bracketed editorial insertions [ענין] and [את פריו] supplied from parallel manuscripts; letter (ה) and vav [ו] are vocalization/orthographic markers in the Hebrew witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:06.397766748Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}